    <Header2>Summary</Header2>
    <Paragraph>
        We've learnt how to build a parser with lalrpop and it was much more pleasant than writing a recursive descent
        parser by hand. Aside from the lexer location issue it was basically frictionless. If you've ever written a parser
        with yacc or Bison then you probably know &ldquo;pleasant&rdquo; and &ldquo;frictionless&rdquo; are not the first
        words that come to mind. In any case, we are now ready for some MLIR!
    </Paragraph>
